<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Donnchad Ua Cerbaill</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1168</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Donough O'Carroll</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Donnchad Ua Cerbaill was king of Airgialla in the north of Ireland in the 12th century. He extended his realm into Louth and was a major supporter of church reform, founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mellifont-abbey">Mellifont Abbey</a> in 1142 with St Malachy, the first Cistercian monastery in Ireland. He was killed in 1168.</p></div>
